<h3 id="rules-that-feel-like-open-with-grew-a-brain">Rules that feel like Open With grew a brain</h3>

<p>For each file type you can:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Prefer specific editors (one or many — open several apps at once)</li>
  <li>Fall back to a Default Rule / Always Open list</li>
  <li>Build When conditions on filename, extension, parent folder, and more</li>
  <li>Pop a <strong>radial</strong> or list picker when you want to choose every time (or only when a rule says so)</li>
  <li>Bind hotkeys to rules so selection in Finder goes straight to the right stack</li>
</ul>


              
